Supply Capacity and Cost Remain Key Challenges

SiC substrates are generally more challenging to manufacture than conventional silicon substrates. Crystal-growth complexity, processing requirements and yield considerations can increase costs and constrain supply.

Device manufacturers must qualify substrates and maintain consistent performance across production lots. Suppliers must also manage capital investment, process improvements and long-term customer relationships.

The market's growth therefore depends not only on demand for SiC devices but also on the industry's ability to improve manufacturing efficiency and material availability.

